        <section>
          <h2 id="summary">Summary</h2>
          <p>This section expands the corrosion model by focusing on formulation-driven mechanisms. Both
            liquid-phase and vapor-phase pathways influence corrosion behavior, while coating performance,
            solvent interactions, pH drift, humidity cycles, and propellant dynamics determine long-term
            stability. Understanding these mechanisms enables more accurate prediction of failure modes and
            supports the engineering of robust water-based aerosol products.</p>
        </section>

